# hyperbolictile

- Label: Hyperbolic Tile
- Category: Copernicus (`Cop`), Houdini 22.0.368
- Inputs: 0 to 1
- Parameters: 10 (exact, read from Houdini by hython)
- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/hyperbolictile.html
- Summary (EN): Generates tiles of hyperbolic regular polygons built in the Poincaré disk model, repeating the base polygon by reflection and inversion. Suits patterns such as ceramics or floor tiles.
- Résumé (FR) : Génère des pavages de polygones hyperboliques réguliers dans le disque de Poincaré, utiles pour des motifs de carrelage.

- Inputs meaning: ["size_ref: reference layer that sets the output image size and metadata"]

- Key parameters: [{"name": "Iterations", "meaning": "how many times the base polygon pattern repeats inside the disk"}, {"name": "Polygons", "meaning": "number of sides on the base polygon"}, {"name": "Rectanglize", "meaning": "replaces the circular boundary with a square, using a chosen mapping type"}, {"name": "Flattening", "meaning": "pushes circular arcs toward the border; at 0 the polygon stays inside the disk"}, {"name": "Size", "meaning": "length of the base polygon straight lines; sets the disk radius when Flattening is 0"}, {"name": "Tile Fitting", "meaning": "how much the image fills each tile in the uv output"}, {"name": "Poincaré Disk Mask", "meaning": "shows only the pattern inside the disk; no effect when Rectanglize is on"}]

- Caveats: ["Each square mapping distorts differently: Conformal shows artifacts near corners, Elliptic Grid stretches near corners, Squircle distorts diagonals more."]

